sk`\n(parsed exactly like `final_answer`), carrying a `questions[]` payload â€” whitelisting **only** the\nliteral `ask` so a still-unknown action keeps returning `null` (the anti-laundering invariant);\nthe loop surfaces it as a terminal result `stop.reason:\"ask\"` with the questions (mirroring\n`final_answer`); a **flag-gated** (`GWL_HARNESS_CLARIFY`) prompt instruction (in the BP2 tier-2 block)\ntelling the reasoner it MAY emit `ask` + the gate policy (ask only when underspecified /\nirreversible-next / calibrated-uncertain; â‰¤3 branch-eliminating questions; else PROCEED). The\n`parseDecision` accept-set change is always-safe; the prompt instruction is the only prefix-affecting\npart and is flag-gated so BP1/BP2 stays byte-identical when off.\n\n**Depends on:** â€”\n\n**done-when:** a decision `{action:\"ask\",questions:[...]}` is parsed + surfaced as a terminal `ask`\nresult; a still-unknown action returns `null`; production `tool_call`/`final_answer` decisions are\nbyte-identical; with the flag OFF the prompt prefix hash is unchanged.\n\n- **Given** `{action:\"ask\",questions:[\"which DB?\"]}`, **when** parsed, **then** the loop terminates with `stop.reason:\"ask\"` and the questions surfaced.\n- **Given** an unknown action (e.g. `\"frobnicate\"`), **when** parsed, **then** it still returns `null` (anti-laundering preserved) and a normal `tool_call`/`final_answer` is byte-identical.\n- **Given** the clarify flag OFF, **when** the prompt is built, **then** the BP1/BP2 prefix hash equals the pre-feature prompt's (assert via `computePrefixHash`).\n\n## Wave 2 â€” C3 Progress narration: one line per observe (from LIVE loop state)\n\n**Intent:** Surface one compressed progress line per observe step, drawn from state the loop ALREADY","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":189}}}
